  "query_preview": "past this evening. \n\nThe main change in the pattern for the extended part of the forecast \nis the progged redevelopment of the upper ridge over the central \nplains by the end of the week and lasting through the weekend. The \nlast several runs of the ECMWF have been consistent in the \nredevelopment of the ridge right over KS and is supported by the 00Z \nGFS and AIGFS. So why WPC/NBM is forecasting highs in the lower to \nmiddle 90s this weekend is puzzling. Cluster analysis of the 12Z \nensembles showed more than 50 percent of the members also have the \ncenter of the upper ridge over the forecast area. And while \nincreasing spreads in the envelop of possible temperatures may \nexplain a gradual cooling trend in the extended forecast, the 01Z NBM\nkeeps highs in the middle and upper 90s for Friday and Saturday in\ncontrast to the WPC forecast. Cluster analysis showed only about 15 \nand 20 percent of the members had a pattern supportive of the cooler \ntemps. Meanwhile the 00Z ECMWF/GFS and 12Z LREF would suggest the \nupper 90s to around 100 heat should persist through next weekend. So \nI think the forecast is a little to optimistic suggesting cooler \ntemps this weekend.",
